    "text": "A satellite of mass<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> &nbsp;is launched vertically upwards with an initial speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math> from the surface of the earth. After it reaches height <math><mi>R</mi></math> ( <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math> radius of the earth), it ejects a rocket of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math> so that subsequently the satellite moves in a circular orbit. The kinetic energy of the rocket is ( <math><mi>G</mi></math> is the gravitational constant; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math> is the mass of the earth):",
